ill definitely want to read more.<br /><br />Lure of the Dragon<br /><br />This is the first book in the author's new paranormal series featuring dragon shifters and other shifters in Hawaii. I love her wolf shifter stories and was excited to see how she would create this new storyline. In addition to Kai, you have other shifters that have banded together to keep others safe from harm. Many of them have been hurt by humans and women and are not sure how much they trust Tessa. I am looking forward to reading their stories as the information we do get on the other characters is intriguing and I definitely want to learn more about them.<br /><br />Rebel Dragon<br /><br />This is another great read from Anna Lowe. It is part of a new series but related to the previous one and has many of my favorite characters back. You probably will want to go read the earlier books once you realize how great a read it is but you don't have to.<br /><br />The author did a wonderful job building the relationship between Jenna and Connor. You get a lot of background that helped me feel like I really understood the characters and why they were making<br />the choices they made. Jenna and Connor have great chemistry from the very beginning.<br /><br />I liked and respected both Jenna and Connor. I felt like they tried to make the best choices for themselves and others and really cared about the people in their life. He has an interesting family both biological and made by friendship. Connor's devotion to his brothers is very admirable.<br /><br />The course of love is not easy. The opening is really good and you feel the foreshadowing of danger. The fear keeps building as you wait for the enemy to make their appearance. There are personal issues too that make him hesitant to pursue her. He wants to do what was right and focus on his job<br />but his dragon really pulls him towards Jenna.<br /><br />The author also does a really good job with developing the other characters too and increasing interest in reading their stories. Cynthia is a really interesting character and hear some of her story Her son helps illustrate a different side to Dell. It definitely make me look forward to hearing their stories. Chase is also a real mystery too especially with how he was raised. I think that will<br />be a very interesting story.<br /><br />I liked the ending and felt it resolved their story but still left room for the other stories. Too many times the author leaves too much open at the end to help bring others to the next books if they want answers. The author doesn't leave the reader with a big cliffhanger but left me with the feeling of looking forward to more.<br /><br />Fire Maidens: Paris<br /><br />Natalie and Tristan are drawn together by love and danger. Natalie has no idea about the other side of the city and that supernaturals exist. Tristan is one of the supernaturals responsible for guarding to the city. He is assigned to be her secret bodyguard on a mission that he doesn't necessarily agree with but one that he feels he can't turn down.<br /><br />The connection between them is intense from that first meeting. I really love how sweet and caring Tristan is towards Natalie. He really is devoted to her happiness and safety. Natalie is someone that is easy to like. She really cares about others and is perfectly suited for her future role.<br /><br />I enjoyed the characters and their story fit Paris perfectly. I am looking forward to the next book. Another great love story in another special city.<br /><br />I am voluntarily reviewing a copy I received.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked